DESIGN PATTERN → LLD/HLD MAPPING (Quick Reference)

Strategy:
- Parking Lot → ParkingStrategy (LowestFloorFirst, NearestToExit)
- Rate Limiter → Algorithm selection (TokenBucket, SlidingWindow)
- Payment → PaymentStrategy (UPI, CreditCard, Wallet)
- Booking System → PricingStrategy (Regular, Weekend, Holiday)
- Online Book Store

Observer:
- Booking System → ShowObserver (notify waitlisted users when seat frees up)
- Chat Messenger → notify group members on new message
- Uber → notify drivers when new ride request comes
- Hospital → alert doctors when critical patient added

State:
- Elevator → IdleState, MovingUp, MovingDown, DoorOpen
- Hospital → Patient states (Registered → InQueue → InConsultation → Discharged)
- Uber → Ride states (Requested → DriverAssigned → InProgress → Completed)
- Booking → Booking states (Pending → Confirmed → Cancelled)

Command:
- Text Editor → Undo/Redo (AppendTextCommand)
- Chess → Move history, undo moves

Factory:
- Parking Lot → SpotFactory (creates CompactSpot, RegularSpot, LargeSpot)
- Booking System → TicketService.generateTicket() (ticket creation logic)
- Notification → NotifierFactory (creates Email/SMS/Push notifier)

Singleton:
- Parking Lot → ParkingLot (one orchestrator)
- Cache → single shared cache
- DB Connection → one connection pool
- Logger → one log stream

Builder:
- Complex configs (URL Shortener config, Search queries, Notifications)

Facade:
- Hospital System → HospitalManagementSystem (hides 4 services)
- Shopping → ShoppingFacade (hides Inventory+Payment+Shipping+Notification)
- Booking System → BookingFacade

Adapter:
- Payment Gateway → RazorpayAdapter, StripeAdapter
- Media Player (your existing code)

KEY LEARNINGS:
- In LLD, classes have getters and setters — mention by name
- Strategy is the MOST asked pattern — know cold
- Observer + Strategy combo appears in almost every LLD
- State pattern replaces messy if-else chains for status management
- Multiple payment options → Strategy